      "defect": "missing-hypothesis",
      "evidence": "The page says the reaction “vanishes on the noncontact set” without a continuity or representative convention. The obstacle definition imposes its inequality on almost-everywhere classes. The scoped complementarity corollary states this conclusion with the additional condition that “u and ψ have continuous representatives,” and Proof 1.2 uses that continuity to make {u>ψ} open. Without such a convention, the pointwise noncontact set is not canonical for general H¹ classes, nor is it specified as an open set on which the distribution vanishes.",
